input.new_string:
  "empyrion",
  // `terraria` is DELIBERATELY absent — researched in depth during the
  // 2026-09-29 mod-install audit, and it stays out for two independent, real
  // reasons rather than "not gotten to yet":
  //
  //  1. The 1000 seeded Terraria `GameMod` rows are all `source: "steam_workshop"`
  //     — real content, but it's tModLoader's Workshop catalogue (tModLoader
  //     itself ships as a separate app, and 1.4+ tModLoader mods are
  //     distributed through Steam Workshop under tModLoader's own listing).
  //     Nxeon's actual Terraria product (prisma/catalog.ts's `terraria`
  //     template) runs `ryshe/terraria`, a VANILLA Terraria + TShock image —
  //     tModLoader is never installed. There is no server-side process that
  //     would ever read a Workshop mod id we wrote anywhere; downloading one
  //     of these 1000 items would just leave an inert file, which is a fake
  //     "installed" state, not a real one. Fixing this for real means
  //     offering a second, tModLoader-based Terraria server variant — a
  //     product decision, not a mechanical wiring job.
  //
  //  2. Even for the content type Nxeon's ACTUAL Terraria server can use —
  //     TShock plugins, real .dll files, typically distributed as GitHub
  //     release assets (which `RESOLVABLE_SOURCES`'s `"github"` entry can
  //     already fetch) — there is nowhere to put one. TShock installs at
  //     `/tshock` inside the `ryshe/terraria` container (see the `terraria`
  //     OsTemplate's own comment in prisma/catalog.ts, sourced from that
  //     image's real `/tshock/bootstrap.sh`), and the template's ONLY bind
  //     mount is `-v /opt/terraria:/root/.local/share/Terraria/Worlds` — the
  //     world-save folder, not TShock's install tree. `/tshock/ServerPlugins`
  //     is not reachable from the host at all today, so neither an automated
  //     installer NOR a customer's own manual "upload it in Files" can
  //     actually reach it — the honest fallback message this module shows is
  //     accurate, but slightly understates the gap (it isn't just "not
  //     automated yet," it's "not reachable yet, automated or not").
  //     A real fix needs a provisioning-script change (bind-mount
  //     `/tshock/ServerPlugins` to a new host path) that MUST be verified
  //     against a real running container before it ships — a host directory
  //     bind-mounted over a path a Docker image populates at build time can
  //     silently blank out whatever was there, so this is not a change to
  //     make blind. Not attempted this pass: no real, permitted way to
  //     provision a live test container was available in this session (see
  //     docs/DOCUMENTATION.md's 2026-09-29 entry for the full account).
]);

